searches/04_dfs_recursive_and_iterative.algorithm:
dfs_recursive(graph, node, seen, order):
    add node to seen, append node to order
    for neighbour in graph[node]:
        if neighbour not in seen: dfs_recursive(graph, neighbour, seen, order)
    return order
dfs_iterative(graph, start):
    order = [], seen = {}, stack = [start]
    while the stack is not empty:
        node = pop the top
        if node in seen: continue   (a stale copy: the node was already reached another way)
        add node to seen, append node to order
        for neighbour in reversed(graph[node]): push neighbour
    return order

